Subject: [PATCH] Avoid checked value access after successful emplacement

Both emplace overloads call value() after constructing the contained object.
This instantiates value()'s explicit throw even though the optional is known
to be engaged, making otherwise non-throwing emplacement fail to compile
with -fno-exceptions.

Return the contained object through operator* instead. Construction and
exception propagation are unchanged; no assignment requirement is added.
This also avoids a redundant engagement check when exceptions are enabled.
---
 include/tl/optional.hpp | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/include/tl/optional.hpp b/include/tl/optional.hpp
--- a/include/tl/optional.hpp
+++ b/include/tl/optional.hpp
@@ -1219,7 +1219,7 @@
 
     *this = nullopt;
     this->construct(std::forward<Args>(args)...);
-    return value();
+    return **this;
   }
 
   template <class U, class... Args>
@@ -1229,7 +1229,7 @@
   emplace(std::initializer_list<U> il, Args &&... args) {
     *this = nullopt;
     this->construct(il, std::forward<Args>(args)...);
-    return value();    
+    return **this;
   }
 
   /// Swaps this optional with the other.
